    name="1 Data Acquisition and Ingestion Value Stream"
    id="id-eb0ec68c1ced4b4d837ee439a787c1bf"
    documentation="Data Acquisition and Ingestion Value Stream&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Purpose:&#xD;&#xA;To acquire, access, or receive raw data from internal or external sources and bring it into the organization’s statistical environment under controlled governance conditions.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Description:&#xD;&#xA;This value stream begins with the identification of data needs and the establishment of agreements with data providers. It encompasses data collection through surveys, administrative registers, sensors, web scraping, or data spaces. The main value contribution is making relevant, high-quality, and authorized data available for statistical use.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;At this stage, value is created through access, trust, and compliance — ensuring that the data entering the system is ethically sourced, legally compliant, and fit for purpose. The resulting artefact is a collected dataset, accompanied by metadata describing source, format, and quality attributes.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Key capabilities: Data Acquisition Management, Source Integration, Data Governance, Security &amp; Privacy Management, Metadata Registration."
    viewpoint="value_stream">
